#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119550 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "b25256b2-09fe-5faa-b27a-bfea7654e8ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-3019" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119551 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "5c4164d7-605a-597c-9bab-f6599becc527" :question/math-academy-id "e-3020" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119552 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "1d356bbb-b4ad-5730-9bd1-7f3cd151f96f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3021" :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119698 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/id #uuid "40927582-03c4-5dcb-b2cc-7c68c73388b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8688" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0549aad0-d3df-5bda-b5ff-a2a28949ce32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-8,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259920} {:answer/id #uuid "9a34877b-0c90-54bc-a15c-e4ef580ff774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261212} {:answer/id #uuid "9fbe6911-5632-5913-a554-2c6c9b2cd4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261260} {:answer/id #uuid "a9dcd6b2-1af9-52b2-863a-f10202e72cc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-6,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261361} {:answer/id #uuid "ad108365-5066-5f63-ba54-eb2a13ec2de6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-5,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fbe6911-5632-5913-a554-2c6c9b2cd4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261260} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e799d64-76f3-5753-a340-9612a01bb001" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "595f95a8-e242-59b0-85cf-ad884a52eaa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-129140" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,-6,\\,3⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afc8add8-a972-543e-ba5d-502649377eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}+1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388001} {:answer/id #uuid "88d76c60-f635-5b53-b9a2-21eb7b22c38d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,\\,\\sqrt{2}-2,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388002} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d13bc7-8fd9-5c74-85e1-35ca1c16399f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-6,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388003} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f9b0d5-b1ef-500e-9a9a-1756568b9eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,\\,5\\sqrt{2}+1,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388004} {:answer/id #uuid "a27359af-1ebf-57f7-a5f2-e6e3c036c4a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a27359af-1ebf-57f7-a5f2-e6e3c036c4a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388005} :answer-field/id #uuid "08002127-d475-5849-b316-13394942fb74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57f0244e-104a-5517-a9c5-a53620a2a15d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129149" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,\\sqrt{2},\\,2⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{4},\\,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=2{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2⟨-3,\\,\\sqrt{2},\\,2⟩+4⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{4},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,\\,2\\sqrt{2},\\,4⟩+⟨-6,\\,-1,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-1,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "475d1e66-6f6e-5029-b393-ac8091e81847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,10,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440586} {:answer/id #uuid "59708d17-ec19-5008-a725-f506623819e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,11,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440590} {:answer/id #uuid "c1f48cd2-7a1e-5567-a774-54e3c2cd766d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,11,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440610} {:answer/id #uuid "c8cf5629-cbfe-56cf-80b8-847fb1feda67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,\\,11,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440611} {:answer/id #uuid "d960990e-be34-50b8-8883-ca8b7c72ab98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,\\,8,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8cf5629-cbfe-56cf-80b8-847fb1feda67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-7,\\,11,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440611} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ee2c23-f39d-50cc-8ad6-40fbb0395dc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fc5a0e9-33d2-5427-a227-a63b18c415e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-129151" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{2}[f(t)+\\frac{5}{3}g(t)]\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,1,\\,4⟩$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,6,\\,0⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}[f(t)+\\frac{5}{3}g(t)]\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{5}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[f(t)+\\frac{5}{3}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{5}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,1,\\,4⟩+\\frac{5}{3}⟨-3,\\,6,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,1,\\,4⟩+⟨-5,\\,10,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,\\,11,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02719984-1eed-5b45-abb8-f9d57dc603d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-13,\\,-5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263020} {:answer/id #uuid "860b18bb-4f4a-53c7-963e-483683ca820f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,\\,-8,\\,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264156} {:answer/id #uuid "ac417052-a513-5339-871c-05eea4809c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,\\,-10,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264479} {:answer/id #uuid "e01c6d3f-0fda-5f52-8740-cb7b48f432c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨15,\\,-2,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264946} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1f1b37-f089-50aa-ae75-d977544c3e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,\\,-12,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac417052-a513-5339-871c-05eea4809c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,\\,-10,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264479} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a9a315-8af0-5512-bbf8-ebf3e0bd6e5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "620fd628-6fe2-5040-9cd0-aaf37f31206b" :question/math-academy-id "q-129268" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{4}^{0}f(t)+⟨3,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,6,\\,0⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,6,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-6,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{0}f(t)+⟨3,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{4}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{0}⟨3,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-6,\\,0⟩+⟨3t,\\,t,\\,-2t⟩{|}_{4}^{0} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-6,\\,0⟩+⟨-12,\\,-4,\\,8⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨-9,\\,-10,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb8259f-8c90-5906-950d-4eceda1af95a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440580} {:answer/id #uuid "3577fefa-4330-511f-bfb5-e3b0bdd5b2d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440585} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb2546e-95e7-5c4f-8882-4b1f0f221022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,3,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440598} {:answer/id #uuid "a45f0695-37ea-5976-9377-b321aab76838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,-5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440601} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf3598f-9c3e-57f6-8286-eee1de57ab13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cb8259f-8c90-5906-950d-4eceda1af95a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440580} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ce4d30d-9663-5cde-be1f-6bc470206c3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47592607-bdfd-5d8e-9c5b-5217893655c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-129271" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨15,\\,3,\\,6⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨12,\\,2,\\,4⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨15,\\,3,\\,6⟩-⟨12,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440628 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23bcd99d-a4d7-5113-8122-b434800d4251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,\\,1,\\,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440582} {:answer/id #uuid "6c26fae9-27e1-5a9e-b8cc-cb6d50822c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,-3,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440594} {:answer/id #uuid "bac614d5-c883-5f75-be5e-9a172f5f740e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,-3,\\,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440606} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd1551e-45c9-59c0-b91f-7e4eb6a9ca61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,3,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440609} {:answer/id #uuid "d231f7b9-7f46-59da-906f-71bc37334995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,\\,3,\\,-6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d231f7b9-7f46-59da-906f-71bc37334995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,\\,3,\\,-6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440613} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fcc12cf-1a92-5a62-8733-9c5f6c91157d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0dd4df5a-0e6b-52af-bfbd-9f8a6a0eb73b" :question/math-academy-id "q-129273" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨6,\\,-2,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{4}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,-1,\\,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{4}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨3,\\,-1,\\,2⟩-⟨6,\\,-2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-9,\\,3,\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440632 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16f5d70b-9eea-5eb4-936b-2c00a263ca0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440577} {:answer/id #uuid "77824988-4246-5cea-8838-bc3d0f779587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440596} {:answer/id #uuid "a89108bd-e5fa-5710-9681-caef88996500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440604} {:answer/id #uuid "e6089965-6e3e-5a22-aa9e-148dc9abdb27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440617} {:answer/id #uuid "e91ca837-f562-5561-8d71-ccbc1a47662d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77824988-4246-5cea-8838-bc3d0f779587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440596} :answer-field/id #uuid "18b293a5-b7ee-51c5-a5dd-f201959d8404" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90fd82d6-81fe-5d91-84c9-583a4bc9e1c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-129288" :question/problem "Given that \n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{e}{2}\\,i+3e\\,j-\\,k,$ \n$c=4\\,i-j+u\\,k,$\nand \n${\\int }_{1}^{3}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ what is the value of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(4\\,i-j+u\\,k)\\cdot (\\frac{e}{2}\\,i+3e\\,j-k) \\\\  & =2e-3e-u \\\\  & =-e-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${\\int }_{1}^{3}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ we must have $-e-u=0,$ which means that $u=-e.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d99e8a1-d9f3-5f82-af54-6968a95a1bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+7\\,j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440573} {:answer/id #uuid "656b4822-846d-53ba-8264-7ca1a6236744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+4\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440592} {:answer/id #uuid "a19efb0d-cd16-5561-9b60-33edcdd0cf62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i+7\\,j-4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440599} {:answer/id #uuid "a3ba84af-5ed3-53ad-87ee-31f41e20153c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i+2\\,j-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440600} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c65bc8-479e-5100-94af-a35f364e4685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i-7\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2c65bc8-479e-5100-94af-a35f364e4685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i-7\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440615} :answer-field/id #uuid "648beb9f-469a-53fa-a29e-23cb1da4aeb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42e2902f-b402-5b6e-826c-93f62fddd9ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-129293" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{5}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=i-j+3\\,k$ \nand \n$c=2\\,i-k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2\\,i-k)\\times (i-j+3\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0-1)i-(6+1)j+(-2-0)k \\\\  & =-i-7\\,j-2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c08ea4b-77bf-5be9-95f7-6f7a1369c182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i+2\\,j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263656} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffc9ed7-eb98-5a8d-b53f-7bb55b6b45aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i-5\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263830} {:answer/id #uuid "bd254509-fcff-5a01-9878-c181c3cd57fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+3\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264642} {:answer/id #uuid "be01fa84-fad6-5ae4-9c1e-a73ae3b28a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i+5\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264651} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1adc9e-0280-54e8-ab23-e88e4d69a7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+5\\,j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef1adc9e-0280-54e8-ab23-e88e4d69a7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+5\\,j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265096} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c3c66d-9b18-5c7a-bf81-ae419bdf2386" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "553c9eff-921e-5636-9757-6a75aa064098" :question/math-academy-id "q-129295" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=i+j-3\\,k$ \nand \n$c=i-j+2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i-j+2\\,k)\\times (i+j-3\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-2)i-(-3-2)j+(1+1)k \\\\  & =i+5\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0735890c-3c78-543f-89dd-6ca5377bb2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,i+17\\,j-12\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440570} {:answer/id #uuid "4be058a2-5710-5ff7-a820-882c2fc11385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,i+7\\,j-24\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440587} {:answer/id #uuid "4eafeb6b-988b-5aa2-8275-39f0afff0b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11\\,i+15\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440588} {:answer/id #uuid "9797327b-29d3-5967-8722-3e2bb5aa98ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\,i+16\\,j-24\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440597} {:answer/id #uuid "a78142dc-7eec-57bb-a2d3-d7dcffeea81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a78142dc-7eec-57bb-a2d3-d7dcffeea81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440603} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd206ea4-1fa4-5b1a-b95a-d7f9dcd15b33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9dfd8a34-cf86-59cc-aba6-9a0a73cfe2af" :question/math-academy-id "q-129296" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=7\\,i-4\\,j-k$ \nand \n$c=3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k)\\times (7\\,i-4\\,j-k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5+8)i-(-3-14)j+(-12+35)k \\\\  & =13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b4f82ad-fdb2-5472-91cf-034c72d89d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,\\,-2,\\,20⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440578} {:answer/id #uuid "28a82d4e-66b8-522b-bb29-15ce2137bdbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,-6,\\,16⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440584} {:answer/id #uuid "617f6a04-b5a3-562e-944b-b155e9ef1135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,6,\\,16⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440591} {:answer/id #uuid "69479ad1-c6b2-5a1b-806d-681f0eb3c7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,6,\\,16⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440593} {:answer/id #uuid "bb058d20-70c9-58d9-8796-636b8520c920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,\\,-6,\\,20⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28a82d4e-66b8-522b-bb29-15ce2137bdbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,-6,\\,16⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440584} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9391d8f-51c6-50ad-a822-94facfbb487b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "936ae073-f786-5498-b379-ef3a0cdfd96d" :question/math-academy-id "q-32496" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[6f(t)-2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,3⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[6f(t)-2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=6{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[6f(t)-2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =6{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,3⟩-2⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-4,\\,18⟩-⟨2,\\,2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-6,\\,16⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c143a77-e1af-52aa-b7eb-98785edc55ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i+2j+24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440571} {:answer/id #uuid "1f61aaf4-763c-5aa0-8b51-415ad9b6527c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j-24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440581} {:answer/id #uuid "56eb2684-dae3-5d7e-affd-236ebbf2899e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i-2j+8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440589} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc32dcc-74ea-50ee-823d-5aefc081089d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i+2j-8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440608} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6245d5-3350-59d5-9f2f-1fe8e4fa79d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j+8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f61aaf4-763c-5aa0-8b51-415ad9b6527c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+2j-24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440581} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac63dd9f-32cd-5ec8-8fb2-52c021ed5db9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e79507a4-566e-5fff-acc4-da31b5f94ddb" :question/math-academy-id "q-32521" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=16\\,i+8\\,j+2\\,k$ \nand \n$c=-i+j.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(-i+j)\\times (16\\,i+8\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 8 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 16 & 8\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(-2-0)j+(-8-16)k \\\\  & =2i+2j-24k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46bf7675-80a2-559b-8162-709a1a0d7f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,\\,6,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358358} {:answer/id #uuid "52b55dd5-256e-5209-86de-a9c9700d2990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,2,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358461} {:answer/id #uuid "90b044f6-737d-5f41-adc8-0bdca392f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359017} {:answer/id #uuid "e6dcc4aa-84e5-52fb-b4ea-896d476393a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359794} {:answer/id #uuid "ec412725-0d94-59a0-8fbf-bf17919c936a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,-3,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90b044f6-737d-5f41-adc8-0bdca392f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359017} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e28b5a-b897-5ddd-a2bd-d85b9a72bf4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29982efe-8588-56f9-8a2e-657a512dab79" :question/math-academy-id "q-96943" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩-⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e985bc-3646-55e6-b3a2-05849e559813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440569} {:answer/id #uuid "0c92cdac-b992-5f56-8073-a74a63b8e267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440572} {:answer/id #uuid "1431b01c-fbae-5eca-ba0e-3973bfffb5d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440575} {:answer/id #uuid "7182028f-2b74-5eac-980c-1d5e909f08df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,-2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440595} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a507f5-177d-52c0-bc32-cfb379389058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,1,\\,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00e985bc-3646-55e6-b3a2-05849e559813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440569} :answer-field/id #uuid "114f26d7-6c07-5fb1-aa45-8dac954ec030" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63279440-ddaa-5ce9-9454-481ab5b36e09" :question/math-academy-id "q-98093" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)+⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-3,\\,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)+⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-3,\\,-4⟩+{⟨t,\\,t,\\,t⟩|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,-3,\\,-4⟩+⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29a4ca46-2d86-5674-925d-0fca36cce902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,6,\\,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395418} {:answer/id #uuid "73270a0c-faaa-5059-903b-a2dbfd94f784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-6,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395419} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd5832f-7dce-5750-ba86-e382d26ba47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,3,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395420} {:answer/id #uuid "292d6f26-5842-5490-9a69-e3d9649895fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395421} {:answer/id #uuid "2312de20-e709-5b80-a27b-d10d7e0e5430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29a4ca46-2d86-5674-925d-0fca36cce902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,\\,6,\\,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395418} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c625c76-a044-5d00-8e7b-aae0bedd3be2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2776fb8a-9df3-5def-8690-2a494e137c16" :question/math-academy-id "q-98096" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}2f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨1,\\,-3,\\,2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨1,\\,-3,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,3,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the scalar multiplication rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,3,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,6,\\,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fa697c9-4d76-5898-8fb5-ac84a77debdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,\\sqrt{3}-3,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395439} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8a89ab-8c73-517f-8e47-53ad9f4c06fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,\\sqrt{3}+1,\\,-12⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395440} {:answer/id #uuid "b9fcf75b-c1d0-5f39-9056-7c5640eb928e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395441} {:answer/id #uuid "1423503f-a4b1-5ae9-ba3b-0e1efa315d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,\\sqrt{3},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395442} {:answer/id #uuid "ab0fdc34-4ee8-516c-b880-42f9c2fcec55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,\\sqrt{3}+1,\\,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab0fdc34-4ee8-516c-b880-42f9c2fcec55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,\\sqrt{3}+1,\\,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395443} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5f819ae-49fc-5c26-94b2-5e3cdd0e1a0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c2ff90f-3df2-5a7a-ae8c-1f49f03b53d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-98170" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{3}[f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,\\sqrt{3}-1,\\,2⟩$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,-\\frac{5}{2}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}[f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}[f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{1}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,\\sqrt{3}-1,\\,2⟩+4⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,-\\frac{5}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,\\sqrt{3}-1,\\,2⟩+⟨3,\\,2,\\,-10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,\\sqrt{3}+1,\\,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits 